#[summary("std::str 차등 시험: 표준 입력의 줄마다 `s\tp`를 읽어 모든 함수의 결과를 찍는다 (tests/stdlib.rs, backlog 4B-02)")]
mod diff {
    #[effects(io)]
    fn opt(r: Option<usize>) -> () {
        match r {
            None => print_str("-\n"),
            Some(i) => print_u64(u64::try_from(i).unwrap()),
        }
    }

    #[effects(io)]
    fn flag(b: bool) -> () {
        if b {
            print_str("1\n");
        } else {
            print_str("0\n");
        }
    }

    // Every function of `std::str` on `s` and `p`, and the character at
    // every byte of `s`.
    #[effects(io)]
    fn show(s: &str, p: &str) -> () {
        flag(s.starts_with(p));
        flag(s.ends_with(p));
        opt(s.find(p));
        opt(s.strip_prefix(p));
        opt(s.strip_suffix(p));
        print_u64(u64::try_from(s.trim_ascii_start()).unwrap());
        print_u64(u64::try_from(s.trim_ascii_end()).unwrap());
        let mut i: usize = 0;
        while i <= s.len()
            decreases s.len() + 1 - i,
        {
            match s.decode_utf8(i) {
                None => print_str("-\n"),
                Some(d) => {
                    print_u64(u64::try_from(u32::from(d.ch)).unwrap());
                    print_u64(u64::try_from(d.next).unwrap());
                }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // A line `s\tp\n`: the two texts, cut at the tab and before the line
    // feed (both ASCII, so both cuts are character boundaries).
    #[effects(io)]
    #[uses(std::bytes::found, std::bytes::at, std::str::found, std::str::ends, std::str::ended)]
    fn one(line: &str) -> () {
        if !line.ends_with("\n") {
            return;
        }
        match line.find("\t") {
            None => {}
            Some(t) => {
                if t < line.len() - 1 {
                    show(&line[0..t], &line[t + 1..line.len() - 1]);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    #[effects(alloc, io, nondet)]
    fn main() -> () {
        let mut n: u64 = 0;
        while n < 1000000
            decreases 1000000 - n,
        {
            let mut line: String = String::new();
            match std::io::read_line(&mut line) {
                Ok(k) => {
                    if k == 0 {
                        n = 1000000;
                    } else {
                        one(line.as_str());
                        n = n + 1;
                    }
                }
                Err(e) => {
                    n = 1000000;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
